{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe eval/calibration surface excludes activated project code-review criteria. `_code_review_prompt_id` only admits the static built-in physical ids and has no repository context (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:187-201`). `calibrate_criterion` maps non-physical ids through the default plan-review namespace and has no code-review membership branch (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:384-421`).\n\n## Approach\n\n- In `eval_solver.py`, change `_code_review_prompt_id` to accept `repo_root` as a keyword argument. Build its admissible physical-id set from the current built-ins plus every logical id returned by `code_review.registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)`, mapped with `criterion_prompt_id(logical_id, gate_key=\"code_review\")`. Pass the existing `_run_code_review_case` `repo_root` into this helper. This pins the logical-to-physical seam (`project.foo` → `code-review-project-foo`) and preserves built-in behavior.\n- In `eval.py`, select the new code-review calibration arm with one explicit predicate: `criterion_id in code_review.registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)`. In that arm resolve the physical prompt via `criterion_prompt_id(criterion_id, gate_key=\"code_review\")`; otherwise retain the existing plan-review branch byte-for-byte.\n- In the code-review arm only, catch `EvalError` from `load_eval_spec` and re-raise a located `EvalError` that includes the logical `criterion_id` and preserves the original path/message. This makes missing project eval assets actionable without changing plan-review errors.\n- Keep the work limited to the resolver/calibration seam and behavioral tests; do not add project-specific special cases.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: in a synthetic repo with active `project.foo`, `_code_review_prompt_id(\"code-review-project-foo\", repo_root=repo_root)` is admitted and calibration runs its code-review eval fixture through `_run_code_review_case`.\n- Mapping edge: inactive project physical ids are rejected, proving admission maps active logical ids to physical ids rather than comparing raw strings.\n- Parity: a plan-review criterion still follows the unchanged plan-review calibration path.\n- Missing spec: an active project code-review logical id with no eval YAML raises `EvalError` containing both `project.foo` and the located eval-spec path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An activated project code-review criterion resolves and calibrates through the code-review arm; verified by `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k eval`.\n- [ ] A plan-review criterion eval path is unchanged; verified by the same `-k eval` selector.\n- [ ] `_code_review_prompt_id(\"code-review-project-foo\", repo_root=repo_root)` admits the active logical `project.foo` mapping and rejects an inactive project id; verified by the same selector.\n- [ ] A project code-review criterion with no eval spec raises a located `EvalError` whose message contains the logical criterion id; verified by the same selector."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1784935220471388001,"uuid":"7e57da42-f11a-4d9f-87ac-a09b59754167"}